---
description: Next.js consumer and admin UI conventions
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Frontend

- Consume the real API. Do not keep a parallel hardcoded product model.
- Deal availability, prices, and verification freshness come from the API.
- Feature folders (`src/features/*`) own feature UI. `src/components` is reusable chrome only.
- Analytics: emit `analytics.track("deal_opened", payload)` — never vendor SDK calls in components.
- Maps/geocoding go through `src/lib/maps.ts`. The list-first UI must work when maps are flagged off.
- Browser geolocation is optional. Neighborhood and city selection must work without it.
- Empty, loading, and error states are designed UI, not raw exception text.
- Do not put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables.
- Prefer server-rendered pages for indexable city/venue routes. Set canonical URLs to findgood.food.
- Admin reliability over polish. Reuse the API client; do not duplicate types.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const isActive = new Date().getHours() >= 15;

// ✅ GOOD
<DealStatusBadge status={deal.availability.status} />
```
